<h2>Where SMA maintenance sits in the statutory map</h2>

<p>Maintenance in Indian law runs on parallel tracks: the personal-law or marriage-statute track, the religion-neutral criminal-procedure track (Section 125 of the Code of Criminal Procedure, 1973, now Section 144 of the Bharatiya Nagarik Suraksha Sanhita, 2023), and the Domestic Violence Act track. For couples married under the Special Marriage Act, the first track runs through Sections 36 and 37 of that Act — provisions that mirror, with differences, Sections 24 and 25 of the Hindu Marriage Act, 1955. The forum in Delhi is the Family Court dealing with the matrimonial case.</p>

<table class="law">
